---Information about a link aggregation group (LAG).
---@class aws.direct_connect.Lag
---@field connectionsBandwidth? aws.direct_connect.Bandwidth The individual bandwidth of the physical connections bundled by the LAG. The possible values are 1Gbps, 10Gbps, 100Gbps, or 400 Gbps..
---@field numberOfConnections aws.direct_connect.Count The number of physical dedicated connections initially provisioned and bundled by the LAG. You can have a maximum of four connections when the port speed is 1 Gbps or 10 Gbps, or two when the port speed is 100 Gbps or 400 Gbps.
---@field lagId? aws.direct_connect.LagId The ID of the LAG.
---@field ownerAccount? aws.direct_connect.OwnerAccount The ID of the Amazon Web Services account that owns the LAG.
---@field lagName? aws.direct_connect.LagName The name of the LAG.
---@field lagState? aws.direct_connect.LagState The state of the LAG. The following are the possible values:
---@field location? aws.direct_connect.LocationCode The location of the LAG.
---@field region? aws.direct_connect.Region The Amazon Web Services Region where the connection is located.
---@field minimumLinks aws.direct_connect.Count The minimum number of physical dedicated connections that must be operational for the LAG itself to be operational.
---@field awsDevice? aws.direct_connect.AwsDevice The Direct Connect endpoint that hosts the LAG.
---@field awsDeviceV2? aws.direct_connect.AwsDeviceV2 The Direct Connect endpoint that hosts the LAG.
---@field awsLogicalDeviceId? aws.direct_connect.AwsLogicalDeviceId The Direct Connect endpoint that terminates the logical connection. This device might be different than the device that terminates the physical connection.
---@field connections? aws.direct_connect.ConnectionList The connections bundled by the LAG.
---@field allowsHostedConnections aws.direct_connect.BooleanFlag Indicates whether the LAG can host other connections.
---@field jumboFrameCapable? aws.direct_connect.JumboFrameCapable Indicates whether jumbo frames are supported.
---@field hasLogicalRedundancy? aws.direct_connect.HasLogicalRedundancy Indicates whether the LAG supports a secondary BGP peer in the same address family (IPv4/IPv6).
---@field tags? aws.direct_connect.TagList The tags associated with the LAG.
---@field providerName? aws.direct_connect.ProviderName The name of the service provider associated with the LAG.
---@field macSecCapable? aws.direct_connect.MacSecCapable Indicates whether the LAG supports MAC Security (MACsec).
---@field encryptionMode? aws.direct_connect.EncryptionMode The LAG MAC Security (MACsec) encryption mode.
---@field macSecKeys? aws.direct_connect.MacSecKeyList The MAC Security (MACsec) security keys associated with the LAG.
---@field prefixPoolSizeIpv4? aws.direct_connect.PrefixPoolSize The total number of inbound IPv4 route prefixes you can allocate across the virtual interfaces on the LAG. Not applicable to LAGs that are interconnects and support hosted connections.
---@field prefixPoolSizeIpv6? aws.direct_connect.PrefixPoolSize The total number of inbound IPv6 route prefixes you can allocate across the virtual interfaces on the LAG. Not applicable to LAGs that are interconnects and support hosted connections.
---@field prefixPoolUnallocatedCountIpv4? aws.direct_connect.PrefixPoolUnallocatedCount The number of inbound IPv4 route prefixes in the LAG prefix pool not yet allocated to a virtual interface. Not applicable to LAGs that are interconnects and support hosted connections.
---@field prefixPoolUnallocatedCountIpv6? aws.direct_connect.PrefixPoolUnallocatedCount The number of inbound IPv6 route prefixes in the LAG prefix pool not yet allocated to a virtual interface. Not applicable to LAGs that are interconnects and support hosted connections.
---@field rateLimiterStatus? aws.direct_connect.RateLimiterStatus The rate limiter status for the LAG, including how many rate limiters are in use and the maximum allowed.
---@field billingMode? aws.direct_connect.BillingMode The billing mode of the LAG.

